Third-party components

The browser play page (play.html) loads the vc64web emulator — mithrendal's
WebAssembly port of Dirk W. Hoffmann's VirtualC64
(https://github.com/dirkwhoffmann/virtualC64), licensed GPL-3.0 — at runtime
from a separate repository (https://github.com/nschneir/vc64web.github.io).
No emulator code is included or distributed in this repository.
The system ROM images the emulator boots on are likewise hosted in
that separate repository, not in this one — and they are not
Commodore's. They are the KERNAL, BASIC and character ROMs of the
MEGA65 open-roms project (https://github.com/MEGA65/open-roms), a
free/libre re-implementation licensed under the GNU Lesser General
Public License, version 3 or later:

    Copyright Paul Gardner-Stephen, 2019.
    Copyright Roman Standzikowski (FeralChild64), 2019-2021.

Some of the BASIC sources those binaries are built from are
additionally under the MIT License, Copyright (c) Microsoft
Corporation. The PXL font in the character ROM is the work of
Retrofan, included in open-roms with permission under the LGPL-3.0.
The full upstream licence text is vendored beside the binaries in the
separate repository as roms/LICENSE-open-roms.txt, with provenance,
SHA-256 pins and the corresponding-source pointer in roms/README.md.

No Commodore ROM image is hosted or distributed by either repository —
the local VICE tooling reads ROM bytes only from the emulator you
install. There is no 1541 drive ROM in the set at all: each demo is
served to the play page as a .prg that the emulator flashes straight
into RAM.
